From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] isa: use the 52-bit class field for plain arm64 on macOS

Apple builds macOS's libobjc for arm64e only, so the packed-isa layout for
arm64 without pointer authentication is iOS's: a 33-bit class field sized
for iOS's 64 GB user address space (MACH_VM_MAX_ADDRESS 0x1000000000).
macOS's user address space is 47 bits, so a plain-arm64 macOS build fails
objc-runtime-new's static assert that ISA_MASK covers MACH_VM_MAX_ADDRESS,
and would truncate class pointers if it didn't. The arm64 simulator,
which is plain arm64 on a macOS address space, already takes the arm64e
layout (52-bit shiftcls_and_sig, unsigned when there is no ptrauth);
plain-arm64 macOS takes it for the same reason. setClass in objc-object.h
repeats the conditional and changes with it.

Rebase-risk: low (two #if conditions).
---
diff --git a/runtime/isa.h b/runtime/isa.h
--- a/runtime/isa.h
+++ b/runtime/isa.h
@@ -57,7 +57,8 @@
 # if __arm64__
 // ARM64 simulators have a larger address space, so use the ARM64e
 // scheme even when simulators build for ARM64-not-e.
-#   if   __has_feature(ptrauth_calls) || TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR
+// NeoDarwin: so does macOS built for ARM64-not-e, for the same reason.
+#   if   __has_feature(ptrauth_calls) || TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR || TARGET_OS_OSX
 #     define ISA_MASK        0x007ffffffffffff8ULL
 #     define ISA_MAGIC_MASK  0x0000000000000001ULL
 #     define ISA_MAGIC_VALUE 0x0000000000000001ULL
diff --git a/runtime/objc-object.h b/runtime/objc-object.h
--- a/runtime/objc-object.h
+++ b/runtime/objc-object.h
@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@
 #endif
 
     // Match the conditional in isa.h.
-#if __has_feature(ptrauth_calls) || TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR
+#if __has_feature(ptrauth_calls) || TARGET_OS_SIMULATOR || TARGET_OS_OSX
 #   if ISA_SIGNING_SIGN_MODE == ISA_SIGNING_SIGN_NONE
     // No signing, just use the raw pointer.
     uintptr_t signedCls = (uintptr_t)newCls;
